      <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Government bonds are generally viewed as one of the safest assets to invest in. That’s because it’s considered relatively unlikely that the issuer — a government — will go bankrupt. Among the world’s major government debt markets, Japan’s $7.5 trillion bond market has, for decades, been considered one of the most stable.</description>
